{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","id":"13e083a2-7f44-43ca-8eae-51efc9097f74","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:17:22.853Z","version":"2.1.317","querySource":"repl_main_thread","shapeHash":"abdbf879f1c8baf4d3d130a8ccbe0672e594508c87565d961c1f493173127f1f","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"557edf9d-4002-4885-957e-b102bc8c2284","keep":225,"tail":["f43be1acb8763e96057e601e30b7489bd20438bf53edb48a1c46b8aa51ca88ed","9049dc845e372fd1644df5c5dd1f0f5e781d4e5b040ae25ccd80d04105550586"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",226,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"42df688e1fb4a6452f3823883f5e159fe2a922b9289c63783f6cf1c1394ba984"}
{"parentUuid":"e530d4e0-48af-4241-9133-e3c62da774f0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj8pYNmfwbx8dG4aW5JX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That's simpler, and it's deterministic. I've recorded it on trail #30 and in Entire Brain.\n\n**The model as I've written it down:**\n- **Value comes from the corpus.** A node's value is how much of the argument rests on it across the whole corpus, the because-ness we defined today. A source's value is the value of the claims its quotes support. A contributor's value is the value of the nodes they added or fixed. All of it can be recomputed from any commit.\n- **Allocation is the MiFID calculation.** I've read that as the MiFID II research-payment approach: set the research budget in advance, then pay it out by a documented assessment of each provider's value. Here the budget is the network margin, and the documented assessment is the graph itself, computed and never scored by hand.\n- **The market research becomes background only.** The $2.2B market and the nonprofit share that was never published don't enter the calculation.\n\n**Two things to settle:**\n- **The central plan says the opposite of part of this.** It says a citation or graph path alone isn't a contribution that earns a payout. A fixed budget handed out by a documented graph assessment may be the answer to that objection, but the plan has to be changed explicitly, not worked around. I've flagged it on the trail.\n- **Counsel.** MiFID II is EU law, and Ethical Capital is a US adviser. The US rules on paying for research (Section 28(e) and the SEC's handling of MiFID research payments) are a question for counsel before any payout, as the plan already requires.\n\nTwo new questions are on the trail:\n- **The value function.** Which graph measure, how it's normalised, and how forks and dissent count. A dissent that turns a check red should earn something too.\n- **The budget.** The period it covers and how it's set.\n\nIs \"MiFID calculation\" the research-payment allocation I described, or did you mean a different MiFID method?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1668,"cache_read_input_tokens":272671,"output_tokens":602,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1668,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":602,"cache_read_input_tokens":272671,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1668,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1668},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e2979e63-bd91-4a24-b539-d1e1b473d078","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgj8pY4fx4JFhzNPyYiWt","requestRef":"13e083a2-7f44-43ca-8eae-51efc9097f74","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"21e7e5ae-42df-4225-977b-72ab3c0d1590","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:17:28.783Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
