{"parentUuid":"dce2e36a-a92c-4188-af82-ed05e63d4010","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9B66nrCx5cNEYMK5HH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":922,"cache_read_input_tokens":280380,"output_tokens":1203,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":383},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":922,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1203,"cache_read_input_tokens":280380,"cache_creation_input_tokens":922,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":922},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":4618,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"9355fdcc-5707-4a72-be5d-18754ef5df99","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgj9B5rf2XserKqT2Gthj","requestRef":"ffc92db8-61fe-4981-8613-3310e2f57835","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"dddb1103-b9e2-4518-9c07-99308b375481","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:22:09.727Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"dddb1103-b9e2-4518-9c07-99308b375481","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9B66nrCx5cNEYMK5HH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01G1isy6pJUfMmPszuzEXCzc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad; cat >> $S/trail-commons.md <<'EOF'\n\nEmbargo licence: direction (Sloane, 2026-11-04)\n- A licensee could create a private data point from our inputs and license us to keep it secret for a period. For example, a hedge fund finds something important to our network in our dataset, but isn't ready to share it.\n- Holding it back is a cost to our objectives, so its price must be computable.\n\nNotes (Claude; proposals):\n- Commit, then reveal. When the finding is made, the licensee deposits it sealed, and its digest goes on our record at once with the date. At the embargo's end it is released to the commons automatically. The commitment proves the finding existed and wasn't altered; the release is part of the contract, not a favour.\n- Price = what the delay costs the network: (the finding's value to the network, computed from the graph like any node: what would rest on it) × (the embargo length), with a rising rate for longer embargoes and a maximum term. Computed, never negotiated case by case, under \"deterministic unless Sloane overrides\".\n- Some findings may not be embargoable at any price: imminent harm to people, or anything the network's safety depends on. That limit should be set before the first embargo, not during one.\n- Counsel, first and hard. Ethical Capital is a registered adviser that manages money. Holding a hedge fund's unreleased finding raises information-barrier and conflict questions, possibly material non-public information depending on what the finding is. Policies and counsel come before any embargo is offered.\n\nFurther questions:\n16. The embargo price function, its maximum term, and what is never embargoable.\n17. Who holds the sealed deposit, and how release is guaranteed if we or the licensee disappear (escrow, or encryption with a time-locked key).\n18. The information-barrier policy for Ethical Capital, with counsel.\nEOF\ncd /Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc && entire trail update 30 --project et/ec1c --body \"$(cat $S/trail-commons.md)\" >/dev/null 2>&1; echo rc=$?","description":"Record the embargo licence on trail #30"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":922,"cache_read_input_tokens":280380,"output_tokens":1203,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":383},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":922,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1203,"cache_read_input_tokens":280380,"cache_creation_input_tokens":922,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":922},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01G1isy6pJUfMmPszuzEXCzc":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad; cat >> $S/trail-commons.md <<'EOF'\n\nEmbargo licence: direction (Sloane, 2026-11-04)\n- A licensee could create a private data point from our inputs and license us to keep it secret for a period. For example, a hedge fund finds something important to our network in our dataset, but isn't ready to share it.\n- Holding it back is a cost to our objectives, so its price must be computable.\n\nNotes (Claude; proposals):\n- Commit, then reveal. When the finding is made, the licensee deposits it sealed, and its digest goes on our record at once with the date. At the embargo's end it is released to the commons automatically. The commitment proves the finding existed and wasn't altered; the release is part of the contract, not a favour.\n- Price = what the delay costs the network: (the finding's value to the network, computed from the graph like any node: what would rest on it) × (the embargo length), with a rising rate for longer embargoes and a maximum term. Computed, never negotiated case by case, under \"deterministic unless Sloane overrides\".\n- Some findings may not be embargoable at any price: imminent harm to people, or anything the network's safety depends on. That limit should be set before the first embargo, not during one.\n- Counsel, first and hard. Ethical Capital is a registered adviser that manages money. Holding a hedge fund's unreleased finding raises information-barrier and conflict questions, possibly material non-public information depending on what the finding is. Policies and counsel come before any embargo is offered.\n\nFurther questions:\n16. The embargo price function, its maximum term, and what is never embargoable.\n17. Who holds the sealed deposit, and how release is guaranteed if we or the licensee disappear (escrow, or encryption with a time-locked key).\n18. The information-barrier policy for Ethical Capital, with counsel.\nEOF\ncd /Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc && entire trail update 30 --project et/ec1c --body \"$(cat $S/trail-commons.md)\" >/dev/null 2>&1; echo rc=$?","description":"Record the embargo licence on trail #30"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"9355fdcc-5707-4a72-be5d-18754ef5df99","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgj9B5rf2XserKqT2Gthj","requestRef":"ffc92db8-61fe-4981-8613-3310e2f57835","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"18f21f9a-b992-46fa-9cbf-afda069b867c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:22:17.897Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"