{"parentUuid":"df9028aa-41f6-4302-871a-9238413b0373","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjBH7W2uZvZCzGXJbGjf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HT9t6N3KeBS3GKb8jMmiE6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad; cat > $S/primitives.md <<'EOF'\n\nPrimitive set (draft, 2026-11-04). Rule (Sloane): before a question goes on a trail, it points at the primitives it concerns. A question that fits no primitive either names a new one or isn't ready.\n- P-pin: a source pinned by bytes and digest\n- P-recipe: a recorded, general way to turn a source into text\n- P-claim: a statement with evidence, or resting on other claims\n- P-graph: the argument as rests_on links; conjunction\n- P-because: because-ness, the value of a node computed from the graph\n- P-check: the deterministic verifier and its result\n- P-circle: concentric circles, of assumption (0 bytes … 4 human) and of access (who may see what). The information-walls policy is this primitive applied to access.\n- P-witness: who or what produced a step, with model and prompt digest\n- P-badge: a citation (durable) or status (expiring) mark of a result\n- P-grant: a signed, scoped, expiring permission (the handshake)\n- P-boundary: in the game or out of it; the scoped box for agents\n- P-contribution: a recorded give-back (fork, support, answer, task, code)\n- P-fork: dissent as a kept branch of the graph against a versioned claim\n- P-question: an open question that graduates into a discussion\n- P-task: work emitted by the check, done when the check turns ok\n- P-price: at cost + firm margin + network margin; the allocation of the network margin\n- P-coverage: loss/coverage, the measure of flattening\n- P-embargo: commit now, reveal at a set date, priced by the delay's cost\nDomain primitives: P-PBC (public benefit corporations), P-Woodcache (the case study).\n\nQuestions pointed at primitives:\n- #29: Q1 use layer → P-grant, P-boundary · Q2 status window → P-badge · Q3 hosting → P-badge · Q4 signing → P-grant, P-witness · Q5 sequencing → P-check, P-badge · Q6 handshake form → P-grant · Q7 commercial line → P-price, P-contribution · Q8 phone package → P-pin, P-claim, P-badge\n- #30: Q1 what counts as a contribution → P-contribution · Q2 what makers receive → P-price · Q3 the question set → P-question · Q4 graph comparison → P-graph, P-fork · Q5 meta-license → P-grant · Q6 extraction measure → P-price, P-boundary · Q7 margin rates → P-price · Q8 agent identity → P-grant, P-boundary · Q9 agent box → P-boundary, P-circle · Q10 task board → P-task, P-check · Q11 value function → P-because, P-graph · Q12 budget → P-price · Q13 CDP test → P-pin, P-coverage · Q14 flattening price → P-coverage, P-price · Q15 enforcement → P-grant, P-pin, P-badge · Q16 embargo price → P-embargo, P-because · Q17 sealed deposit → P-embargo, P-circle · Q18 information walls → P-circle (answered in direction: the walls policy is concentric circles of access)\nEOF\npython3 -I - \"$S\" <<'EOF'\nimport sys\nS=sys.argv[1]; p=f\"{S}/trail-commons.md\"; s=open(p,encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\na=\"18. The information-barrier policy for Ethical Capital, with counsel.\"\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,\"18. The information-barrier policy: direction (Sloane, 2026-11-04). It is concentric circles, applied to access: rings of who may see what, with the embargoed finding in an inner ring until release. Counsel still reviews the rings for Ethical Capital's duties as an adviser.\")\ns+=open(f\"{S}/primitives.md\",encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\nopen(p,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\nt=open(f\"{S}/trail-badges2.md\",encoding=\"utf-8\").read()+\"\\n(Questions on this trail are pointed at primitives on trail #30, \\\"Primitive set\\\".)\\n\"\nopen(f\"{S}/trail-badges2.md\",\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\").write(t)\nEOF\ncd /Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc && entire trail update 30 --project et/ec1c --body \"$(cat $S/trail-commons.md)\" >/dev/null 2>&1; echo rc30=$?; entire trail update 29 --project et/ec1c --body \"$(cat $S/trail-badges2.md)\" >/dev/null 2>&1; echo rc29=$?","description":"Draft the primitive set, point every trail question at it, and record walls as circles"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":609,"cache_read_input_tokens":282516,"output_tokens":2388,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":667},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":609,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2388,"cache_read_input_tokens":282516,"cache_creation_input_tokens":609,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":609},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HT9t6N3KeBS3GKb8jMmiE6":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad; cat > $S/primitives.md <<'EOF'\n\nPrimitive set (draft, 2026-11-04). Rule (Sloane): before a question goes on a trail, it points at the primitives it concerns. A question that fits no primitive either names a new one or isn't ready.\n- P-pin: a source pinned by bytes and digest\n- P-recipe: a recorded, general way to turn a source into text\n- P-claim: a statement with evidence, or resting on other claims\n- P-graph: the argument as rests_on links; conjunction\n- P-because: because-ness, the value of a node computed from the graph\n- P-check: the deterministic verifier and its result\n- P-circle: concentric circles, of assumption (0 bytes … 4 human) and of access (who may see what). The information-walls policy is this primitive applied to access.\n- P-witness: who or what produced a step, with model and prompt digest\n- P-badge: a citation (durable) or status (expiring) mark of a result\n- P-grant: a signed, scoped, expiring permission (the handshake)\n- P-boundary: in the game or out of it; the scoped box for agents\n- P-contribution: a recorded give-back (fork, support, answer, task, code)\n- P-fork: dissent as a kept branch of the graph against a versioned claim\n- P-question: an open question that graduates into a discussion\n- P-task: work emitted by the check, done when the check turns ok\n- P-price: at cost + firm margin + network margin; the allocation of the network margin\n- P-coverage: loss/coverage, the measure of flattening\n- P-embargo: commit now, reveal at a set date, priced by the delay's cost\nDomain primitives: P-PBC (public benefit corporations), P-Woodcache (the case study).\n\nQuestions pointed at primitives:\n- #29: Q1 use layer → P-grant, P-boundary · Q2 status window → P-badge · Q3 hosting → P-badge · Q4 signing → P-grant, P-witness · Q5 sequencing → P-check, P-badge · Q6 handshake form → P-grant · Q7 commercial line → P-price, P-contribution · Q8 phone package → P-pin, P-claim, P-badge\n- #30: Q1 what counts as a contribution → P-contribution · Q2 what makers receive → P-price · Q3 the question set → P-question · Q4 graph comparison → P-graph, P-fork · Q5 meta-license → P-grant · Q6 extraction measure → P-price, P-boundary · Q7 margin rates → P-price · Q8 agent identity → P-grant, P-boundary · Q9 agent box → P-boundary, P-circle · Q10 task board → P-task, P-check · Q11 value function → P-because, P-graph · Q12 budget → P-price · Q13 CDP test → P-pin, P-coverage · Q14 flattening price → P-coverage, P-price · Q15 enforcement → P-grant, P-pin, P-badge · Q16 embargo price → P-embargo, P-because · Q17 sealed deposit → P-embargo, P-circle · Q18 information walls → P-circle (answered in direction: the walls policy is concentric circles of access)\nEOF\npython3 -I - \"$S\" <<'EOF'\nimport sys\nS=sys.argv[1]; p=f\"{S}/trail-commons.md\"; s=open(p,encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\na=\"18. The information-barrier policy for Ethical Capital, with counsel.\"\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,\"18. The information-barrier policy: direction (Sloane, 2026-11-04). It is concentric circles, applied to access: rings of who may see what, with the embargoed finding in an inner ring until release. Counsel still reviews the rings for Ethical Capital's duties as an adviser.\")\ns+=open(f\"{S}/primitives.md\",encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\nopen(p,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\nt=open(f\"{S}/trail-badges2.md\",encoding=\"utf-8\").read()+\"\\n(Questions on this trail are pointed at primitives on trail #30, \\\"Primitive set\\\".)\\n\"\nopen(f\"{S}/trail-badges2.md\",\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\").write(t)\nEOF\ncd /Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc && entire trail update 30 --project et/ec1c --body \"$(cat $S/trail-commons.md)\" >/dev/null 2>&1; echo rc30=$?; entire trail update 29 --project et/ec1c --body \"$(cat $S/trail-badges2.md)\" >/dev/null 2>&1; echo rc29=$?","description":"Draft the primitive set, point every trail question at it, and record walls as circles"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"4696cd30-4b26-4c36-8a5c-99b14f198082","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgjBH7AgkE56Cpau6hVJ2","requestRef":"c5effce9-9cac-4e4b-a9b2-83c676fc5d33","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c689cab4-1583-4f17-9416-1d3704b054a8","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:50:08.249Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
