{"parentUuid":"dde2bcb6-e738-47de-be21-e1af86b24dc0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjBKXv2ELV2WDT7dQNCL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013MxusC19iw5tiWi3gNLCMQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np=\"docs/editorial-standard.md\"; s=open(p,encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\na=\"explaining it again in passing. A primitive page is written once and used\\nby every document that needs it.\\n\"\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,a+\"\"\"\n**Questions point at primitives.** Before an open question goes on a trail\nor into a ledger, it names the primitives it concerns (Sloane, 2026-11-04).\nA question that fits no primitive either names a new primitive or isn't\nready. The draft primitive set is on Entire trail #30 (\"Primitive set\"):\nmethod primitives such as pin, claim, graph, because-ness, check, circle,\nbadge, grant, fork, question and embargo, and domain primitives such as\npublic benefit corporations and the Woodcache case study.\n\"\"\")\nopen(p,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\np=\"docs/comments-standard.md\"; s=open(p,encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\na=\"- An open question about the subject goes into the paper's §8.1, with the\\n  comment's ledger id.\"\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,\"- Every open question first names the primitives it concerns\\n  (`docs/editorial-standard.md`, \\\"Questions point at primitives\\\").\\n\"+a)\nopen(p,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\nEOF\ngit add docs/editorial-standard.md docs/comments-standard.md && printf '%s\\n' \"Standards: open questions point at primitives before they go on a trail\" \"\" \"The draft primitive set is on Entire trail #30; every question on trails\" \"#29 and #30 is now pointed at it. Information walls are concentric circles\" \"applied to access.\" \"\" \"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" > /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b0