{"parentUuid":"f286a69d-c22d-4407-9669-010aa5cfde39","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc/docs/editorial-standard.md","snippet":"","rereadEntry":{"timestamp":1793854221740,"contentHash":"ft49tfd4wvmb","contentLength":6727}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"cb165fc9-23e3-47ec-a832-fa056ab87719","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:50:26.237Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc/docs/editorial-standard.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. The changes are not shown here; use Read if you need the current content.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","hash":"c81438502072c3516d38cc695e9526bdaa97b7107188b2820e70ce83d992bfcd","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now putting the rule into the standards, so it binds future questions, not just these."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013MxusC19iw5tiWi3gNLCMQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np=\"docs/editorial-standard.md\"; s=open(p,encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\na=\"explaining it again in passing. A primitive page is written once and used\\nby every document that needs it.\\n\"\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,a+\"\"\"\n**Questions point at primitives.** Before an open question goes on a trail\nor into a ledger, it names the primitives it concerns (Sloane, 2026-11-04).\nA question that fits no primitive either names a new primitive or isn't\nready. The draft primitive set is on Entire trail #30 (\"Primitive set\"):\nmethod primitives such as pin, claim, graph, because-ness, check, circle,\nbadge, grant, fork, question and embargo, and domain primitives such as\npublic benefit corporations and the Woodcache case study.\n\"\"\")\nopen(p,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\np=\"docs/comments-standard.md\"; s=open(p,encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\na=\"- An open question about the subject goes into the paper's §8.1, with the\\n  comment's ledger id.\"\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,\"- Every open question first names the primitives it concerns\\n  (`docs/editorial-standard.md`, \\\"Questions point at primitives\\\").\\n\"+a)\nopen(p,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\nEOF\ngit add docs/editorial-standard.md docs/comments-standard.md && printf '%s\\n' \"Standards: open questions point at primitives before they go on a trail\" \"\" \"The draft primitive set is on Entire trail #30; every question on trails\" \"#29 and #30 is now pointed at it. Information walls are concentric circles\" \"applied to access.\" \"\" \"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" > /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad/msg14.txt && git commit -q -F /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad/msg14.txt && git push -q origin ec-ai-corpus && git log --oneline -1; entire brain remember \"Open questions must point at primitives before going on a trail; a question fitting no primitive names a new one or isn't ready. Information-walls policy = concentric circles applied to access. Draft primitive set on Entire trail #30 (Sloane 2026-11-04).\" --path workflow.questions.primitives --agent none --json 2>&1 | grep -m1 '\"id\"'","description":"Add the questions-point-at-primitives rule to the standards, commit, push, record"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
