{"parentUuid":"36d1a489-461d-4fec-8fda-2655e60d1432","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjBTMwEL1jPoC3TRBXDs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've made case studies a class, so Woodcache becomes one case among many rather than a primitive of its own. Every case page gets the same three parts:\n1. **What's interesting** about it.\n2. **How it connects to other things:** themes, other cases and claims. Each link carries a weight computed from the graph.\n3. **Your personal connection, if there is one,** stated as a disclosure. For example, you co-founded Woodcache PBC, which the paper already discloses.\n\nI also added two primitives on trail #30:\n- **Theme:** an idea that cuts across cases and ties them together. Your example is technological fetishism, trying to buy the big shiny thing, which links carbon removal to AI and beyond. Public benefit corporations become a theme page too, linked from every PBC case.\n- **Disclosure:** a personal connection, stated wherever it applies.\n\nSo a reader can enter through a case, follow a theme to other cases in completely different fields, and always see where the author has a stake. The standard (`docs/editorial-standard.md`) now says this; committed and pushed as `f0e9111`.\n\nTechnological fetishism is the first theme on the list, with carbon removal and AI as its first two cases. I haven't written any case or theme pages yet; they're for the workspace."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1544,"cache_read_input_tokens":287402,"output_tokens":408,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1544,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":408,"cache_