{"parentUuid":"af8e54a9-5214-4bdc-86d4-892200b53a54","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjC5g2uGPNDgsCVFvLQ9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've started turning it into a Praxis resource. An agent is drafting it in my scratch folder now. I'll review the draft before anything goes into Praxis.\n\n**What the resource is built from:**\n- The syllabus PDF itself is lost. The source is the mental-models corpus that was built from it, `mental-models-comprehensive-v5.md` (843 lines).\n- Nine week titles also survive, from \"Week 01 — Property Before Portfolio\" to \"Week 17 — Capstone II\".\n\n**What the draft will contain:**\n- `README.md` sets out what the resource is and how to use it in a Harkness seminar: each model is a question you put on the table. It includes the surviving week outline, linked to the models each week uses. The missing weeks (02–04, 06–08, 13 and 15) are named as missing, not reconstructed.\n- `models.md` holds the models, kept word for word from the corpus with their attributions. Voss, Meadows, Valentine, Schloss, Napier and the other sources stay credited as the corpus credits them.\n- `PROVENANCE.md` records the source file's SHA-256, a list of everything removed and why, and a note that an LLM did the transformation, so it waits for your review.\n\n**What gets stripped:** the firm's business-model section, anything about Ethical Capital's commercial operations or clients, and internal workflow and tooling notes.\n\n**Before it goes public:**\n- **Jason's agreement.** The Voss models and \"Voss & Ortel (2015)\" are his or co-written.\n- **Where it lands in Praxis.** I'll put it in a new folder of its own (e.g. `praxis/resources/mental-models/`), committing only those files. Praxis has no remote, so committing there doesn't publish anything. Making it public is a separate step, after your review and Jason's agreement."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_se