{"parentUuid":"0ca896ba-0d42-44e7-959c-dc26a9f8c5e6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d1fcd60a-2f37-4659-bf29-bdaae1557aa2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WVzFaVmhMzR51VVsTv8dZw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\n705:| **No Discovery Process (Schwager)** | Jumping into strategy without testing if it fits? | Read → experiment → see what clicks → paper trade → small money → scale. Must discover your fit, nobody can tell you. |\n| 5 | Subtitle \"Ethical Capital Investment Framework\" | Brands the document as the firm's own framework. |\n| 7 | Version line | Version-history detail; recorded here instead. |\n| 24 | \"in our investing?\" | Internal framing; changed to \"in investing?\". The only in-line edit. |\n| 29-49 | Table of contents | Rewritten to match what remains. Source line 44 had three entries run together, including XIc. |\n| 527-535 | XIc. Ethical Capital Business Model (The 3 Ps; Financial Adviser as Life Coach; Analyst's 3 Rights; When Uncertain: Client First; Leverage Amplifies) | The firm's commercial model and client service. Removed whole, as briefed. \"Analyst's 3 Rights\" and \"Leverage Amplifies\" (both source \"Unknown\") are general and could be restored elsewhere if Sloane wants them. |\n| 707-724 | XV. Scoring Guidelines | Instructions for maintaining the author's own copy (\"empirically tested by me\", \"personal track record\"). A one-line note on blank cells replaces it. |\n| 734-735 | \"Update model accuracy based on outcome\"; \"Add learnings to this document\" | Document-maintenance steps. |\n| 745-754 | XVI Quarterly Review | Duplicates XII Quarterly Portfolio Review; its last two items are document maintenance. |\n| 756-763 | XVI Annual Calibration | Document maintenance. |\n| 767-775 | Revision Log | Version history. |\n| 779-840 | \"Quick Summary: What's New in v5.0\" | Version-history summary. It also numbers the leverage points 1-12 in the reverse order of the main Meadows table (it calls \"Constants/Numbers\" #1), which contradicts section VIIIA. |\n| 844 | Closing line (\"This is a working document... A field manual.\") | A note about maintaining the source document. |\n\n## Kept\n\n- Sections I to XIb, XII, XIII, XIV and the \"After Each Position Exit\" list of XVI, with every model's name, question, action, score and source attribution as the source gives them.\n- The tier rankings, labelled as the source author's ranking.\n- Ortel-specific (IX) and Voss-specific (X) models, attributed to Ortel and Voss.\n- XI. Ethical Capital-Specific Models (Veil of Ignorance Test; Harm Reduction Hierarchy; Systems Change > Individual Change; \"Apart From That, Mrs. Lincoln…\"; \"Don't Just Do Something, See Something\"). These are decision models attributed to Ethical Capital, not its commercial operations. The source marks two as Relevance \"Mandatory\"; that label is kept as written.\n- Meadows, Valentine, Schloss, Napier, Carlson, Damodaran, Brakke, Kroijer, Schwager and Klement content, with attribution.\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"be21d4ec-1f6b-4767-bc27-f1e4177dc81e","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:04:56.415Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"1\n705:| **No Discovery Process (Schwager)** | Jumping into strategy without testing if it fits? | Read → experiment → see what clicks → paper trade → small money → scale. Must discover your fit, nobody can tell you. |\n| 5 | Subtitle \"Ethical Capital Investment Framework\" | Brands the document as the firm's own framework. |\n| 7 | Version line | Version-history detail; recorded here instead. |\n| 24 | \"in our investing?\" | Internal framing; changed to \"in investing?\". The only in-line edit. |\n| 29-49 | Table of contents | Rewritten to match what remains. Source line 44 had three entries run together, including XIc. |\n| 527-535 | XIc. Ethical Capital Business Model (The 3 Ps; Financial Adviser as Life Coach; Analyst's 3 Rights; When Uncertain: Client First; Leverage