{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","id":"83375b13-c226-4aca-8844-ac1c76a13909","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:11:55.920Z","version":"2.1.317","querySource":"repl_main_thread","shapeHash":"057cedc1f727758eac2aa8e2c7eab6e54ccaa77bb701c8037a06b043f3aeea83","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"1e85b7d4-a855-4137-8b32-2945c0893b7f","keep":373,"tail":["f2bced0d5ff3c1eeb95c8102cd6cacf7bbc15f7918bae05189b413c29a7cb317","3e5264841f439608990ff3c2493a9d4a14462023d3740f6dde8e21293d09b651"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",374,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"636e1d967014839f5ac7d5cfdf2f16dd96fd3ba9615f5539768beb39eb7d1e91"}
{"parentUuid":"bf57e4d7-0ee6-469f-944b-a472aedf52f7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCyp35ELXDjsX8hckSj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ENDmyxrzwo5HUYTd2B6i6f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad/routing/README.md","content":"# Instruction routing: one place in, the right place out\n\nSloane instructs in one place, and each instruction should flow to where it\nbelongs without her naming the destination (Sloane, 2026-11-04). This folder is\nthe test for that.\n\n## The test\n\n- `instructions.tsv`: 121 distinct instructions Sloane dictated in a single\n  session (2026-11-03 to 2026-11-05), extracted from the session transcript.\n  Dictation artifacts are kept as spoken.\n- `gold.tsv`: where each instruction ought to go under the rules below. These\n  labels are LLM-proposed (circle 3), and under \"deterministic unless Sloane\n  overrides\" they stand once Sloane corrects them. Corrections go in place, and\n  each one is recorded in the commit message.\n- `route_check.py`: scores any router's output against `gold.tsv`. It is red\n  if a privileged instruction is routed anywhere without `dark` (a leak).\n  Otherwise it reports exact matches and per-destination recall and precision.\n\nThere is no router yet, so the test is red by construction. A router passes by\nrouting, not by being fitted to these rows: the rows are a test set, never\ntraining data for a hand-tuned rule (\"checks are not beaten\").\n\n## Destinations and rules\n\n| Destination | Takes |\n|---|---|\n| `dark` | anything privileged (pricing, margins, compensation, licensing terms, enforcement, embargoes, counsel or regulatory matters, named counterparties and asks, clients); the central plan and sequencing |\n| `anthropic-pbc` | the Anthropic paper, its claims, sources, errata and corpora |\n| `praxis` | design and standards shared by every producer: templates, presentation, badge design, primitives, resources, the producer contract, dataset tooling |\n| `descartes` | the checker: quotes, recipes, sealing, verification rules, witness format |\n| `trail` | durable, non-privileged cross-repo intent awaiting decisions |\n| `memory` | a durable rule or preference, recorded beside wherever it acts |\n| `agents-config` | how agents behave across all repos |\n| `tray` | a rendered thing for Sloane to look at |\n| `infra` | compute and infrastructure |\n| `ack` | a go-ahead; it applies to the pending action |\n| `search` | a request to find something |\n\nPrivileged content goes to `dark` even when it concerns another repo as well.\n\n## Known misroutes in the source session\n\nThese are why the test exists. The errata first went to Praxis; Sloane moved\nthem to the paper's repo. Privileged commons economics first went to Entire\ntrails; under the rule adopted later that session, they moved to the dark\nrepo.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1300,"cache_read_input_tokens":369921,"output_tokens":1023,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1300,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1023,"cache_read_input_tokens":369921,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1300,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1300},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01ENDmyxrzwo5HUYTd2B6i6f":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad/routing/README.md","content":"# Instruction routing: one place in, the right place out\n\nSloane instructs in one place, and each instruction should flow to where it\nbelongs without her naming the destination (Sloane, 2026-11-04). This folder is\nthe test for that.\n\n## The test\n\n- `instructions.tsv`: 121 distinct instructions Sloane dictated in a single\n  session (2026-11-03 to 2026-11-05), extracted from the session transcript.\n  Dictation artifacts are kept as spoken.\n- `gold.tsv`: where each instruction ought to go under the rules below. These\n  labels are LLM-proposed (circle 3), and under \"deterministic unless Sloane\n  overrides\" they stand once Sloane corrects them. Corrections go in place, and\n  each one is recorded in the commit message.\n- `route_check.py`: scores any router's output against `gold.tsv`. It is red\n  if a privileged instruction is routed anywhere without `dark` (a leak).\n  Otherwise it reports exact matches and per-destination recall and precision.\n\nThere is no router yet, so the test is red by construction. A router passes by\nrouting, not by being fitted to these rows: the rows are a test set, never\ntraining data for a hand-tuned rule (\"checks are not beaten\").\n\n## Destinations and rules\n\n| Destination | Takes |\n|---|---|\n| `dark` | anything privileged (pricing, margins, compensation, licensing terms, enforcement, embargoes, counsel or regulatory matters, named counterparties and asks, clients); the central plan and sequencing |\n| `anthropic-pbc` | the Anthropic paper, its claims, sources, errata and corpora |\n| `praxis` | design and standards shared by every producer: templates, presentation, badge design, primitives, resources, the producer contract, dataset tooling |\n| `descartes` | the checker: quotes, recipes, sealing, verification rules, witness format |\n| `trail` | durable, non-privileged cross-repo intent awaiting decisions |\n| `memory` | a durable rule or preference, recorded beside wherever it acts |\n| `agents-config` | how agents behave across all repos |\n| `tray` | a rendered thing for Sloane to look at |\n| `infra` | compute and infrastructure |\n| `ack` | a go-ahead; it applies to the pending action |\n| `search` | a request to find something |\n\nPrivileged content goes to `dark` even when it concerns another repo as well.\n\n## Known misroutes in the source session\n\nThese are why the test exists. The errata first went to Praxis; Sloane moved\nthem to the paper's repo. Privileged commons economics first went to Entire\ntrails; under the rule adopted later that session, they moved to the dark\nrepo.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"69448c86-6737-4464-b67f-9ddd879af513","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgjCyoogEdYW3t3nBYRdq","requestRef":"83375b13-c226-4aca-8844-ac1c76a13909","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e8d329ed-7db7-4061-9348-1e4c01aa520f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:12:06.031Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
