{"parentUuid":"9f1b2da4-6976-4a8d-ad5c-35f2ac1ee746","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjD8CWPxLATnZSv16PxL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've set up the test you described: you instruct in one place, and it checks whether each instruction lands in the right place. It's in the dark repo, since that's where the central plan lives, on branch `claude/instruction-routing` under `docs/coordination/instruction-routing/`. A copy is in `~/tray/instruction-routing/`.\n\n**What's in it:**\n- **The test set:** 121 distinct instructions you dictated this session, pulled verbatim from the transcript. It lives in the dark repo because some of them are privileged.\n- **The answer key** (`gold.tsv`): where each instruction *should* go, by rule. An agent labelled them, so under your determinism rule they're a proposal until you correct them. The destinations are:\n  - the three repos: anthropic-pbc, Praxis, Descartes;\n  - the dark repo;\n  - an Entire trail;\n  - memory;\n  - cross-repo agent configuration;\n  - the tray;\n  - infrastructure;\n  - a plain go-ahead;\n  - a search.\n\n  An instruction can go to more than one place.\n- **The scorer** (`route_check.py`): it fails if any privileged instruction ends up outside the dark repo. Otherwise it reports how often each destination is found correctly and how often it's wrong. Right now it fails by construction, because there's no router yet. Against the answer key itself it passes, so the scorer works.\n\n**What the labels show:**\n- **Spread:** 47 instructions belong to anthropic-pbc, 35 to Praxis, 18 to the dark repo, 18 to Descartes, and 34 also carry a rule to remember.\n- **Today's two known misroutes are encoded the right way:**\n  - the errata go to the paper's repo, then roll up to Praxis;\n  - the commons economics (licensing, pricing, flattening, the embargo, The Shareholder Commons) go to the dark repo.\n- **16 instructions can't be routed from their text alone.** They're short follow-ups like \"strip it out\" or \"extract that\". A router has to see the conversation they belong to, so the test checks context too, not just keywords.\n\n**What's not built is the router itself.** I'd make it a model that proposes a destination for each instruction, checked by deterministic rules: anything that looks privileged goes to the dark repo whatever the model says. It's only trusted once it passes this test. The test instructions are for scoring only, never for tuning the router, so it can't just memorize them.\n\nThe five labels the agent was least sure of are the best place to start correcting. For example, I032 (\"tight controls around display and mangling of information\") could be about quote checking or about secrets. Should I build the router next, or do you want to correct those labels first?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1050,"cache_read_input_tokens":375061,"output_tokens":934,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":58},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1050,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":934,"cache_read_input_tokens":375061,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1050,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1050},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"a59203e4-b3f4-48e3-b3fb-08857619ecfd","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgjD8CDYHLphHf2aVHa7E","requestRef":"99af4464-3aed-47e8-94b6-fd94073a9281","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c66cba6e-28c1-4667-b995-2d2eb6aabb22","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:14:00.072Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","e