rType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"bb3e742f-6c6d-415d-93f8-fed0e3cdd063","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b332a665-a152-463b-867b-815cac8956f6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YMFUrLH91AQejAQYJubmv7","type":"tool_result","content":"# Internal Dark planning\n\nThe existing `dark` database on pg-hel1 now holds the first seven operator work\nitems, three prerequisites and ten initial audit events in `planning`. This is\nan intentionally small internal slice, authorized by Sloane on 2026-11-04 while\nthe independent PostgreSQL 18 deployment progresses. It does not activate Auth\nor migrate the rest of the master plan.\n\n`schema.sql` is a one-time migration, not a reset: an existing schema makes it\nfail. `seed.sql` captures the initial work, not a repeatable overwrite. Run both\nin one transaction with `check.sql` before commit. The rehearsal rolled back;\nthe subsequent commit and all three member readbacks succeeded: 7 items, 3\ndependencies, 10 events, and no `dark_auth` schema access.\n\nGenerate the current view with the existing operator SSH access:\n\n```sh\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 infra/dark-plan/plan.py > docs/coordination/current-plan.md\n```\n\nThe view is a read-only snapshot. SQL owns these items' state and priority;\nEntire owns trail/change/review/merge observations. There is no automatic sync,\nnew daemon, login credential, public endpoint or extra database server.\n\nFor an operator state update, execute a transaction as `dark_owner` through the\nexisting administrator transport and call\n`planning.set_state(item_id, expected_revision, next_state, evidence)`.\nA stale revision fails; verified state requires nonempty evidence. Evidence text\nis an operator assertion, not automatic proof. Validate actual acceptance and\nprerequisites before calling it. Direct table access is trusted operator access;\nthis is not a multi-user authorization API. Keep mutations serialized through\nthe operator; concurrent graph-writer acceptance remains future work.\n\n`check.sql` tests stale revision, evidence requirement, dependency-cycle refusal,\ninitial blockers and Auth exclusion. Run fixture checks only in a transaction\nthat rolls back or against a fresh rehearsal; counts and revisions intentionally\nrefer to the original seed. Live replication readback is not backup/restore or\nHA-failover proof. The renderer refuses a known writer that has become a standby;\nautomatic writer discovery is not implemented.\n\nRemaining work belongs to trail #4: import remaining obligations with source\nmapping, reconcile priority writers, narrow runtime access, expected-revision\nedits for other fields, dependency deletion history, and a consistent export and\nrestore rehearsal before retiring the historical plan. The initial operator\naudit does not defend against administrator tampering. Deployment and backup\nwork stays with the database owner; migrating `planning` must preserve IDs,\nrevisions, dependencies and events. No source PDF or private payload is stored\nhere. Keep this internal view out of public mirrors.\n\n\n# Current Dark plan\n\nGenerated read-only snapshot; edit authoritative SQL records, not this view.\nObserved: 2026-11-05T05:15:18.14396+00:00. Internal operator scope. Initial slice only.\n\n## etl-plan-linkage — Trace work outcomes through ETL runs to catalog outputs and consumers\n\nPriority 1 · proposed · revision 16 · [trail #11](https://entire.com/et/ec1c/-/trails/11)\nOwner: unassigned\nReason: Higher-order organization must remain linked to lower-order execution\nUnverified prerequisites: none recorded (not proof of readiness)\nAcceptance: Trace work item to recipe/run/attempt, inputs/outputs, catalog and report; evaluate DuckLake change feed for version-bound invalidation with idempotent replay, durable checkpoints, retention-gap recovery, schema changes and forbidden-target denial. Preserve external metadata; no automatic rewriting of approved reports. Map catalog/table/row IDs to global entity and source-native IDs; verify lineage through compaction/update and explicit remapping on re-import; test inline/file transitions with idempotent change-feed invalidation. Central resource/version/representation IDs must persist through draft, review, approved-version publication, withdrawal, rename, repack and re-encryption. Test stale approval, partial publication, idempotent delivery and permission-filtered links; encryption never grants publication. Store/register admitted original and build authorized local text/metadata search independently of Descartes signing. Verify phrase search and exact original retrieval before signature; later observations link exact source version and locators; signing failure preserves discoverability with honest status. Wire capability-gap producer and persistent receiver through existing runner transport; no unsupported event or false successful result. Verify delivery receipt, duplicates, failed receiver and authorized resume; link diagnostics to the implementing module and owning work item. Runner can emit bounded graph-enrichment proposals even on successful jobs: requirements/capabilities/entities/relations/tests/evaluations with provenance, scope, receiver and dedup identity. Persist proposal separately from job outcome; accepted authority, not emission, changes graph or blockers. Generalize the shared gap/proposal contract to every emitter, retaining source locators, unresolved IDs and relation intent. Persist priority evidence and affected work for central scoring; unresolved citations remain visible and unverified, not dropped or automatically fetched. Reuse Descartes assertion intake via a thin producer adapter, not another assertion/review engine. Receive durable intake and graph IDs; test related-entity suggestions, deduplication, contradictions, failed delivery and projection back to catalog/work items. Intake receipt is not DAG acceptance.\nEvidence: Official DuckLake stable 1.1 docs reviewed: data_change_feed, row_lineage, access_control, backups_and_recovery, data_inlining, expire_snapshots. Source-backed candidate only; no DuckLake runtime trial or migration proved. See infra/dark-plan/README.md. Owner-linked DuckLake inlining, row-lineage and data-types docs reviewed; acceptance in infra/dark-plan/README.md. Documentation evidence only, not deployed behavior. Owner encryption/attribution/lifecycle direction and DuckLake encryption/Shaper upstream docs reviewed; contract in infra/dark-db/storage-access.md#encryption-attribution-and-publication-lifecycle. Proposed acceptance, no runtime adoption. Owner clarified original-search versus observation-attestation separation. Contract: infra/dark-db/storage-access.md#original-retrieval-precedes-observation-attestation; runtime acceptance pending. Inspected dark.jobs events/task and Praxis report writer requirements/init/legacy option. Owner capability-gap, metadata generation/verification and SVG reuse requirements recorded in infra/dark-plan/README.md; implementation pending. Owner requests runner-discovered graph additions and requirement-to-software evaluation. Contract in infra/dark-plan/README.md#runner-proposals-that-enrich-the-graph; implementation pending. Owner confirms all-emitter missing-entity reporting and quantitative importance. Proposed scoring/uncertainty contract: infra/dark-plan/README.md#any-producer-missing-entity-reports-and-importance; not calibrated or implemented. Owner selects Descartes for shared assertion intake, relatedness and importance evaluation. Reviewed Descartes primitives/epistemics design; evaluation runtime support remains to verify. Contract: infra/dark-plan/README.md#descartes-owns-assertion-intake-and-relatedness-evaluation. Owner requires centrally named target groups and communicating work/intake queues, with Descartes automatic on new things. Source verified existing dark.form13f.adv and dark.entity.resolve_filers, Praxis catalog work index and distribution/process_events outbox. Added investment-adviser profile and population-intake-descartes-loop-v1 workflow. Existing outbox queues intents only; no automatic verification execution claimed. This is a specified integration, not a deployed loop. Owner clarifies automatic Descartes intake chiefly establishes chain of custody and enables later issue verification, not truth. Added automatic_intake_assurance contract: exact bytes, source/acquisition, transformations, storage/readback and scoped receipts; incomplete links retain partial evidence and create deduplicated artifact-version-bound verification work. Later resolution appends evidence without rewriting intake history. Runtime remains unconnected. Implemented mise run conformance: four cross-repository fixture tests traverse media/search, catalog registration, event fan-out, archive readback and planning receipt validation. Replay repairs absent catalog view/interrupted fan-out; stale updates, corruption and queued-but-unexecuted Descartes cannot pass. Command passed locally. Complete local component suites total 119 passing tests including four handoffs. Full acceptance remains partial: pinned offline PyYAML 6.0.2 unavailable (catalog ran with 6.0.3); planning suite missing blake3. Actual Descartes worker, live DB handoff in the synthetic test, shared storage, remote delivery and scheduled recovery unverified. Run receipt intake-conformance:20261105:1 recorded; scripts/conformance/README.md documents scope. Added runnable requirement-to-test matrix: scripts/conformance/requirements.json and coverage.py, exposed through mise conformance:coverage. Current 18 scenarios: 6 tested at local boundary, 6 partial, 6 missing. Four mapped tests pass; strict completeness probe exits 1 correctly. Selected implementation hashes and test output in tray coverage.json. This is not line/branch coverage, exhaustive scope or live acceptance.\n\n## external-metadata — Preserve external metadata and source-declared relationships during ingestion\n\nPriority 1 · proposed · revision 12 · [trail #11](https://entire.com/et/ec1c/-/trails/11)\nOwner: unassigned\nReason: Owner requires external metadata and linkages to survive normalization\nUnverified prerequisites: none recorded (not proof of readiness)\nAcceptance: Round-trip source IDs/namespaces/versions, authors, rights, timestamps, citations and typed relationships; metadata-only corrections create attributable versions; unknown fields and unresolved targets survive; no automatic remote fetch or widening access Version source-to-DuckLake-to-export type mappings; test decimal precision, integer bounds, timezone/precision, null versus absent, nested unknown fields and leading-zero IDs; preserve units/currency/schema; reject unrecorded lossy coercion. Verify format 1.1 compatibility for PostgreSQL variant inlining. Preserve creator/publisher/rights and source attribution separately from hashes and encryption; distinguish stored-ciphertext digests from logical content digests and keep restricted linkage metadata protected. Generate deterministic metadata from actual source/build; distinguish source-extracted and inferred fields with per-field provenance. Independently recompute hashes and validate schema/IDs/source assertions; unknown remains unknown; never fabricate authorship, rights or approval. Early bounded pilot: use the existing interview/media records as seeds, preserve source attribution and exact quotations, enable authorized original search before Descartes attestation. Resolve the canonical database field before new discovery scraping; compare existing website media entries rather than recreate the list.\nEvidence: LocalFileStore persists payload only; commit_plan returns digests and calls on_item with item key/digest only. Fabric catalog upsert replaces the nested fetch object through a shallow merge. Verify consumer-owned manifests before claiming metadata preservation. Owner-linked DuckLake inlining, row-lineage and data-types docs reviewed; acceptance in infra/dark-plan/README.md. Documentation evidence only, not deployed behavior. Owner encryption/attribution/lifecycle direction and DuckLake encryption/Shaper upstream docs reviewed; contract in infra/dark-db/storage-access.md#encryption-attribution-and-publication-lifecycle. Proposed acceptance, no runtime adoption. Inspected dark.jobs events/task and Praxis report writer requirements/init/legacy option. Owner capability-gap, metadata generation/verification and SVG reuse requirements recorded in infra/dark-plan/README.md; implementation pending. Media pilot: owner confirmed existing website collection as seed. Corrected count: 20 media records plus one landing page. scripts/ingest/media.py reuses Dark parser and Praxis lexical engine; local generation /Users/srvo/dev/praxis/search/.state/media-intake-20261104 preserves exact originals and source metadata, one labelled draft, and 130 provisional person/organization/topic/attribution relations with exact spans. All 20 original hashes and 130 spans read back; person/topic retrieval and identical replay passed; three focused tests include positive/negative retrieval and changed-generation refusal. Bundle SHA256 d0b060ae948239dc9a1951bd98e3a688aacdcba701e3d36caa3818228eadd59a. Bounded literal vocabulary is not exhaustive entity extraction. Upstream full text/transcripts, embeddings, lake/catalog admission, canonical entity resolution, Descartes signing and live-search deployment remain outstanding. Source and run instructions: scripts/ingest/README.md.\n\n## operator-access — Prove restricted operator storage authorization\n\nPriority 1 · ready · revision 5 · [trail #10](https://entire.com/et/ec1c/-/trails/10)\nOwner: unassigned\nReason: Classification alone does not enforce access\nUnverified prerequisites: none recorded (not proof of readiness)\nAcceptance: Explicit principal/destination mapping; authorized read and denied unauthorized read Apply explicit public/restricted payload and metadata boundaries: no extra payload-confidentiality requirement for genuinely public content; protect private annotations and catalog keys. Validate DuckLake encryption-mode, inline/metadata and backup exposure.\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"205c6afa-851a-4a0d-8d15-17a6fc642d9d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:15:18.837Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Internal Dark planning\n\nThe existing `dark` database on pg-hel1 now holds the first seven operator work\nitems, three prerequisites and ten initial audit events in `planning`. This is\nan intentionally small internal slice, authorized by Sloane on 2026-11-04 while\nthe independent PostgreSQL 18 deployment progresses. It does not activate Auth\nor migrate the rest of the master plan.\n\n`schema.sql` is a one-time migration, not a reset: an existing schema makes it\nfail. `seed.sql` captures the initial work, not a repeatable overwrite. Run both\nin one transaction with `check.sql` before commit. The rehearsal rolled back;\nthe subsequent commit and all three member readbacks succeeded: 7 items, 3\ndependencies, 10 events, and no `dark_auth` schema access.\n\nGenerate the current view with the existing operator SSH access:\n\n```sh\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 infra/dark-plan/plan.py > docs/coordination/current-plan.md\n```\n\nThe view is a read-only snapshot. SQL owns these items' state and priority;\nEntire owns trail/change/review/merge observations. There is no automatic sync,\nnew daemon, login credential, public endpoint or extra database server.\n\nFor an operator state update, execute a transaction as `dark_owner` through the\nexisting administrator transport and call\n`planning.set_state(item_id, expected_revision, next_state, evidence)`.\nA stale revision fails; verified state requires nonempty evidence. Evidence text\nis an operator assertion, not automatic proof. Validate actual acceptance and\nprerequisites before calling it. Direct table access is trusted operator access;\nthis is not