{"parentUuid":"344716e4-23c9-4532-be3a-751079f47fff","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDG4dbN81tMssZVtsdt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The central plan already has a slot for this, item structured-intake-workflow-v1, and only the coordinator writes to it, so I'll re-point the routing test at plan items and write that handoff.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1084,"cache_read_input_tokens":390603,"output_tokens":2594,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":500},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1084,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2594,"cache_read_input_tokens":390603,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1084,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1084},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"89c8ccd4-1467-4914-9d88-e425304642fa","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgjDG4PDAT7VBjtpfyBHM","requestRef":"20e57992-cd92-4757-8918-93c2283033ed","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"215f42b2-20ae-4675-ba55-0719d67337b1","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:15:45.859Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"215f42b2-20ae-4675-ba55-0719d67337b1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDG4dbN81tMssZVtsdt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Dkumq6efnRMXXEyswxcGvA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad; R=$S/routing; python3 -I - \"$R/README.md\" <<'EOF'\nimport sys\np=sys.argv[1]; s=open(p,encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\na=\"## The test\\n\"\ns=s.replace(a,\"\"\"## First hop: the central plan\n\nAn instruction goes to the central plan first, not straight to a repository.\nThe plan's authoritative records are the SQL work items in Dark's `planning`\nschema (rendered read-only as `docs/coordination/current-plan.md`), with\n`praxis-master-plan.md` for sequencing. A router's first output is the work\nitem an instruction amends, or a proposed new item. The repositories are where\nthat work then executes: the second hop, which the destinations below score.\n\nExisting items that today's instructions map onto (observed 2026-11-05):\n\n| Plan item | Trail | Takes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `structured-intake-workflow-v1` | #4 | this routing test itself: owner-requested intake |\n| `inbox-first` | #15 | the one place Sloane instructs from |\n| `report-package` | | the Anthropic paper: claims, errata, rendering, verification chain |\n| `sustainability-opportunity-model` | #24 | pricing, margins, the commons economics (privileged) |\n| `partner-publication-pathways` | | directed asks and partners, e.g. The Shareholder Commons (privileged) |\n| `software-organization-lineage` | | primitives, themes and cases linking to the wider Praxis universe |\n| `praxis-management-home` | | the operator's management surface |\n\nThe plan has one coordinator writer. Agents return a reconciliation handoff\n(`HANDOFF.md`) rather than writing plan records themselves.\n\n## The test\n\"\"\",1)\nopen(p,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\nEOF\ncat > $R/HANDOFF.md <<'EOF'\n# Reconciliation handoff for the plan coordinator, 2026-11-05\n\nFrom the anthropic-pbc session of 2026-11-03 to 2026-11-05. Under \"Close the\nexecution loop\", the coordinator writes plan records; this lists what to\nreconcile and where. None of it has been written to `planning`.\n\n| Plan item | Proposed evidence or amendment | Where the work is |\n|---|---|---|\n| `structured-intake-workflow-v1` (#4) | Owner direction: instruct in one place; each instruction flows to the right place. A routing test exists (121 real instructions, gold labels as an LLM proposal, a scorer that is red on any privileged leak). No router yet. | dark-monocloud branch `claude/instruction-routing` |\n| `sustainability-opportunity-model` (#24) | Owner direction on commons economics: a per-credit price of at-cost sustainability plus a firm margin and a network margin; reciprocity as the commercial line; graph-computed allocation (MiFID-style); flattening raises the price; embargo licences. All are proposals; counsel and ADV come first. | branch `claude/commons-economics-privileged`, `docs/coordination/commons-economics-2026-11-04.md` |\n| `partner-publication-pathways` | Owner direction: The Shareholder Commons is top of the directed asks; the ask itself is undefined. | same file |\n| `report-package` | The paper now has §9 Errata, a generated verification appendix (Appendix F), §0 encoded as argument rows (the thesis fails; 5 premises unsourced), and standards for comments, editorial practice, badges and argument checking. | anthropic-pbc `ec-ai-corpus` (pushed) |\n| `software-organization-lineage` | A draft primitive set, including case, theme, disclosure and missing-file stubs. | Entire trail #30 |\n| new, proposed | A Praxis mental-models seminar resource (Harkness course with Jason Voss). The syllabus PDF is lost; held content is in the private repo. Release waits on Sloane's review and Jason's agreement. | praxis `resources/mental-models` (local, `ec6edbf`); held content in `claude/commons-economics-privileged` |\n\nUnmerged branches for the coordinator: dark-monocloud `claude/commons-economics-privileged`, `claude/instruction-routing`; Descartes `witness-prompt-digest`.\nEOF\ncd /Users/srvo/dev/dark-monocloud && export GIT_INDEX_FILE=$S/ridx && git read-tree 750250118e39 && for f in README.md HANDOFF.md; do B=$(git hash-object -w $R/$f); git update-index --add --cacheinfo 100644,$B,docs/coordination/instruction-routing/$f; done && T=$(git write-tree) && printf '%s\\n' \"docs(coordination): routing goes to the central plan first; reconciliation handoff\" \"\" \"Instructions route first to Dark planning work items, then to repositories.\" \"HANDOFF.md lists what the plan coordinator should reconcile; no planning\" \"records were written.\" \"\" \"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" > $S/rmsg2.txt && P=$(git ls-remote origin refs/heads/claude/instruction-routing | cut -f1) && C=$(git commit-tree \"$T\" -p \"$P\" -F $S/rmsg2.txt) && unset GIT_INDEX_FILE && git push -q origin \"${C}:refs/heads/claude/instruction-routing\" 2>&1 | grep -v checkpoint | tail -1; git ls-remote origin refs/heads/claude/instruction-routing | cut -c1-12; cp $R/README.md $R/HANDOFF.md ~/tray/instruction-routing/","description":"Point the routing test at central plan items, write the coordinator handoff, push","timeout":180000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1084,"cache_read_input_tokens":390603,"output_tokens":2594,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":500},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1084,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2594,"cache_read_input_tokens":390603,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1084,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1084},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Dkumq6efnRMXXEyswxcGvA":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad; R=$S/routing; python3 -I - \"$R/README.md\" <<'EOF'\nimport sys\np=sys.argv[1]; s=open(p,encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\na=\"## The test\\n\"\ns=s.replace(a,\"\"\"## First hop: the central plan\n\nAn instruction goes to the central plan first, not straight to a repository.\nThe plan's authoritative records are the SQL work items in Dark's `planning`\nschema (rendered read-only as `docs/coordination/current-plan.md`), with\n`praxis-master-plan.md` for sequencing. A router's first output is the work\nitem an instruction amends, or a proposed new item. The repositories are where\nthat work then executes: the second hop, which the destinations below score.\n\nExisting items that today's instructions map onto (observed 2026-11-05):\n\n| Plan item | Trail | Takes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `structured-intake-workflow-v1` | #4 | this routing test itself: owner-requested intake |\n| `inbox-first` | #15 | the one place Sloane instructs from |\n| `report-package` | | the Anthropic paper: claims, errata, rendering, verification chain |\n| `sustainability-opportunity-model` | #24 | pricing, margins, the commons economics (privileged) |\n| `partner-publication-pathways` | | directed asks and partners, e.g. The Shareholder Commons (privileged) |\n| `software-organization-lineage` | | primitives, themes and cases linking to the wider Praxis universe |\n| `praxis-management-home` | | the operator's management surface |\n\nThe plan has one coordinator writer. Agents return a reconciliation handoff\n(`HANDOFF.md`) rather than writing plan records themselves.\n\n## The test\n\"\"\",1)\nopen(p,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\nEOF\ncat > $R/HANDOFF.md <<'EOF'\n# Reconciliation handoff for the plan coordinator, 2026-11-05\n\nFrom the anthropic-pbc session of 2026-11-03 to 2026-11-05. Under \"Close the\nexecution loop\", the coordinator writes plan records; this lists what to\nreconcile and where. None of it has been written to `planning`.\n\n| Plan item | Proposed evidence or amendment | Where the work is |\n|---|---|---|\n| `structured-intake-workflow-v1` (#4) | Owner direction: instruct in one place; each instruction flows to the right place. A routing test exists (121 real instructions, gold labels as an LLM proposal, a scorer that is red on any privileged leak). No router yet. | dark-monocloud branch `claude/instruction-routing` |\n| `sustainability-opportunity-model` (#24) | Owner direction on commons economics: a per-credit price of at-cost sustainability plus a firm margin and a network margin; reciprocity as the commercial line; graph-computed allocation (MiFID-style); flattening raises the price; embargo licences. All are proposals; counsel and ADV come first. | branch `claude/commons-economics-privileged`, `docs/coordination/commons-economics-2026-11-04.md` |\n| `partner-publication-pathways` | Owner direction: The Shareholder Commons is top of the directed asks; the ask itself is undefined. | same file |\n| `report-package` | The paper now has §9 Errata, a generated verification appendix (Appendix F), §0 encoded as argument rows (the thesis fails; 5 premises unsourced), and standards for comments, editorial practice, badges and argument checking. | anthropic-pbc `ec-ai-corpus` (pushed) |\n| `software-organization-lineage` | A draft primitive set, including case, theme, disclosure and missing-file stubs. | Entire trail #30 |\n| new, proposed | A Praxis mental-models seminar resource (Harkness course with Jason Voss). The syllabus PDF is lost; held content is in the private repo. Release waits on Sloane's review and Jason's agreement. | praxis `resources/mental-models` (local, `ec6edbf`); held content in `claude/commons-economics-privileged` |\n\nUnmerged branches for the coordinator: dark-monocloud `claude/commons-economics-privileged`, `claude/instruction-routing`; Descartes `witness-prompt-digest`.\nEOF\ncd /Users/srvo/dev/dark-monocloud && export GIT_INDEX_FILE=$S/ridx && git read-tree 750250118e39 && for f in README.md HANDOFF.md; do B=$(git hash-object -w $R/$f); git update-index --add --cacheinfo 100644,$B,docs/coordination/instruction-routing/$f; done && T=$(git write-tree) && printf '%s\\n' \"docs(coordination): routing goes to the central plan first; reconciliation handoff\" \"\" \"Instructions route first to Dark planning work items, then to repositories.\" \"HANDOFF.md lists what the plan coordinator should reconcile; no planning\" \"records were written.\" \"\" \"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" > $S/rmsg2.txt && P=$(git ls-remote origin refs/heads/claude/instruction-routing | cut -f1) && C=$(git commit-tree \"$T\" -p \"$P\" -F $S/rmsg2.txt) && unset GIT_INDEX_FILE && git push -q origin \"${C}:refs/heads/claude/instruction-routing\" 2>&1 | grep -v checkpoint | tail -1; git ls-remote origin refs/heads/claude/instruction-routing | cut -c1-12; cp $R/README.md $R/HANDOFF.md ~/tray/instruction-routing/","description":"Point the routing test at central plan items, write the coordinator handoff, push","timeout":180000}},"serverClassifierRequest":"89c8ccd4-1467-4914-9d88-e425304642fa","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgjDG4PDAT7VBjtpfyBHM","requestRef":"20e57992-cd92-4757-8918-93c2283033ed","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"123b2b36-75cc-43dc-bea8-62ccbf4263a3","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:16:01.970Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version