{"parentUuid":"49867066-3baa-4b97-845b-2fd5de3ca5f8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDRcYVTvArNXAUYoydE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Understood: no plan writes, and the router has to be deterministic. One way in, one fixed path, one way out, so every route can be explained. I'm rescoping the test around that."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":724,"cache_read_input_tokens":395295,"output_tokens":2624,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":687},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":724,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2624,"cache_read_input_tokens":395295,"cache_creation_input_tokens":724,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":724},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"540790d6-39c2-4bbf-ba85-0f155d32d591","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgjDRcAQxjVuio9F52qaj","requestRef":"a9ef7727-ae16-4edb-8398-9002877932de","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"baf03541-16fb-4eb5-875e-017f03eb5281","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:17:57.123Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"baf03541-16fb-4eb5-875e-017f03eb5281","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDRcYVTvArNXAUYoydE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EiraHnK126sV72pLoDrVYG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad; R=$S/routing; python3 -I - \"$R\" <<'EOF'\nimport sys\nR=sys.argv[1]\np=f\"{R}/README.md\"; s=open(p,encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\na=\"## First hop: the central plan\\n\"\ns=s.replace(a,\"\"\"## Scope: determinism\n\nThe point is explainability, so routing must have no randomness (Sloane,\n2026-11-05). One entry point, one path, one output: the same instruction in\nthe same state always routes the same way, and every route can say why.\n\n- **Routing is a pure function.** `route(instruction, context) → (plan item,\n  destinations, rule ids)`. No model makes or breaks a routing decision.\n- **Its inputs are explicit keys, never guesses.** In order:\n  1. a key the instruction carries (a plan item, primitive, claim label or\n     repository it names);\n  2. the context it arrives in: the plan item or thread it replies to, which\n     resolves short follow-ups such as \"strip it out\";\n  3. a versioned lexicon that maps terms to primitives (for example \"margin\",\n     \"embargo\", \"licence\" → privileged primitives).\n- **Rules are fixed and ordered, and each has an id.** The first rule is that\n  anything touching a privileged primitive goes to `dark`. Every route carries\n  the ids of the rules that fired: that list is its explanation.\n- **What resolves to no key is not guessed.** It goes to one `unrouted` queue\n  for Sloane. Her answer is an editorial override, recorded as hers, and it can\n  add a lexicon term or a key, so the same case routes itself next time.\n- **A model may propose keys**, shown as a proposal beside the instruction. The\n  routing never reads it until Sloane accepts it.\n\n## First hop: the central plan\n\"\"\",1)\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"There is no router yet, so the test is red by construction.\"\"\",\"\"\"There is no router yet, so the test is red by construction. The scorer also\nrequires a `rules` column on every routed row (no explanation, no route), and\nwith `--router CMD` it runs the router twice and fails unless both outputs are\nbyte-identical.\"\"\")\nopen(p,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\nEOF\npython3 -I - \"$R/route_check.py\" <<'EOF'\nimport sys\np=sys.argv[1]; s=open(p,encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\ns=s.replace('''def main():\n    gold = load(sys.argv[1])\n    try:\n        pred = load(sys.argv[2])\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        print(f\"RED: no router output at {sys.argv[2]}; {len(gold)} gold rows waiting\")\n        return 1\n''','''def unexplained(path):\n    \"\"\"Rows routed without the rule ids that produced the route.\"\"\"\n    with open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        head = f.readline().rstrip(\"\\\\n\").split(\"\\\\t\")\n        if \"rules\" not in head:\n            return [\"(no rules column)\"]\n        i, r = head.index(\"id\"), head.index(\"rules\")\n        return [c[i] for c in (l.rstrip(\"\\\\n\").split(\"\\\\t\") for l in f) if len(c) <= r or not c[r].strip()]\n\n\ndef deterministic(cmd, instructions):\n    \"\"\"Run the router twice on the same input; outputs must be byte-identical.\"\"\"\n    import subprocess\n    a = subprocess.run(cmd + [instructions], capture_output=True).stdout\n    b = subprocess.run(cmd + [instructions], capture_output=True).stdout\n    return a == b and len(a) > 0\n\n\ndef main():\n    args = sys.argv[1:]\n    router = None\n    if \"--router\" in args:\n        k = args.index(\"--router\")\n        router, args = args[k + 1].split(), args[:k] + args[k + 2:]\n    gold = load(args[0])\n    try:\n        pred = load(args[1])\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        print(f\"RED: no router output at {args[1]}; {len(gold)} gold rows waiting\")\n        return 1\n    bad = unexplained(args[1])\n    if bad:\n        print(\"RED: routes without rule ids:\", \", \".join(bad[:10]))\n        return 1\n    if router and not deterministic(router, args[2] if len(args) > 2 else \"instructions.tsv\"):\n        print(\"RED: router output differs between two runs on the same input\")\n        return 1\n''')\ns=s.replace(\"python3 route_check.py gold.tsv predicted.tsv\",\"python3 route_check.py gold.tsv predicted.tsv [instructions.tsv] [--router 'CMD']\")\nopen(p,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\nEOF\ncd $R && python3 -I route_check.py gold.tsv router-output.tsv; python3 -I route_check.py gold.tsv gold.tsv | tail -1; sed 's/\\trule\\t/\\trules\\t/' gold.tsv > /tmp/x 2>/dev/null; awk 'BEGIN{FS=OFS=\"\\t\"} NR==1{$3=\"rules\"}1' gold.tsv > $S/g2.tsv && python3 -I route_check.py gold.tsv $S/g2.tsv | tail -1","description":"Add the determinism scope to the README and make the scorer require explanations and reproducibility"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":724,"cache_read_input_tokens":395295,"output_tokens":2624,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":687},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":724,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2624,"cache_read_input_tokens":395295,"cache_creation_input_tokens":724,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":724},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01EiraHnK126sV72pLoDrVYG":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-srvo-dev-anthropic-pbc/c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475/scratchpad; R=$S/routing; python3 -I - \"$R\" <<'EOF'\nimport sys\nR=sys.argv[1]\np=f\"{R}/README.md\"; s=open(p,encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\na=\"## First hop: the central plan\\n\"\ns=s.replace(a,\"\"\"## Scope: determinism\n\nThe point is explainability, so routing must have no randomness (Sloane,\n2026-11-05). One entry point, one path, one output: the same instruction in\nthe same state always routes the same way, and every route can say why.\n\n- **Routing is a pure function.** `route(instruction, context) → (plan item,\n  destinations, rule ids)`. No model makes or breaks a routing decision.\n- **Its inputs are explicit keys, never guesses.** In order:\n  1. a key the instruction carries (a plan item, primitive, claim label or\n     repository it names);\n  2. the context it arrives in: the plan item or thread it replies to, which\n     resolves short follow-ups such as \"strip it out\";\n  3. a versioned lexicon that maps terms to primitives (for example \"margin\",\n     \"embargo\", \"licence\" → privileged primitives).\n- **Rules are fixed and ordered, and each has an id.** The first rule is that\n  anything touching a privileged primitive goes to `dark`. Every route carries\n  the ids of the rules that fired: that list is its explanation.\n- **What resolves to no key is not guessed.** It goes to one `unrouted` queue\n  for Sloane. Her answer is an editorial override, recorded as hers, and it can\n  add a lexicon term or a key, so the same case routes itself next time.\n- **A model may propose keys**, shown as a proposal beside the instruction. The\n  routing never reads it until Sloane accepts it.\n\n## First hop: the central plan\n\"\"\",1)\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"There is no router yet, so the test is red by construction.\"\"\",\"\"\"There is no router yet, so the test is red by construction. The scorer also\nrequires a `rules` column on every routed row (no explanation, no route), and\nwith `--router CMD` it runs the router twice and fails unless both outputs are\nbyte-identical.\"\"\")\nopen(p,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\nEOF\npython3 -I - \"$R/route_check.py\" <<'EOF'\nimport sys\np=sys.argv[1]; s=open(p,encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\ns=s.replace('''def main():\n    gold = load(sys.argv[1])\n    try:\n        pred = load(sys.argv[2])\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        print(f\"RED: no router output at {sys.argv[2]}; {len(gold)} gold rows waiting\")\n        return 1\n''','''def unexplained(path):\n    \"\"\"Rows routed without the rule ids that produced the route.\"\"\"\n    with open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        head = f.readline().rstrip(\"\\\\n\").split(\"\\\\t\")\n        if \"rules\" not in head:\n            return [\"(no rules column)\"]\n        i, r = head.index(\"id\"), head.index(\"rules\")\n        return [c[i] for c in (l.rstrip(\"\\\\n\").split(\"\\\\t\") for l in f) if len(c) <= r or not c[r].strip()]\n\n\ndef deterministic(cmd, instructions):\n    \"\"\"Run the router twice on the same input; outputs must be byte-identical.\"\"\"\n    import subprocess\n    a = subprocess.run(cmd + [instructions], capture_output=True).stdout\n    b = subprocess.run(cmd + [instructions], capture_output=True).stdout\n    return a == b and len(a) > 0\n\n\ndef main():\n    args = sys.argv[1:]\n    router = None\n    if \"--router\" in args:\n        k = args.index(\"--router\")\n        router, args = args[k + 1].split(), args[:k] + args[k + 2:]\n    gold = load(args[0])\n    try:\n        pred = load(args[1])\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        print(f\"RED: no router output at {args[1]}; {len(gold)} gold rows waiting\")\n        return 1\n    bad = unexplained(args[1])\n    if bad:\n        print(\"RED: routes without rule ids:\", \", \".join(bad[:10]))\n        return 1\n    if router and not deterministic(router, args[2] if len(args) > 2 else \"instructions.tsv\"):\n        print(\"RED: router output differs between two runs on the same input\")\n        return 1\n''')\ns=s.replace(\"python3 route_check.py gold.tsv predicted.tsv\",\"python3 route_check.py gold.tsv predicted.tsv [instructions.tsv] [--router 'CMD']\")\nopen(p,\"w\",encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\nEOF\ncd $R && python3 -I route_check.py gold.tsv router-output.tsv; python3 -I route_check.py gold.tsv gold.tsv | tail -1; sed 's/\\trule\\t/\\trules\\t/' gold.tsv > /tmp/x 2>/dev/null; awk 'BEGIN{FS=OFS=\"\\t\"} NR==1{$3=\"rules\"}1' gold.tsv > $S/g2.tsv && python3 -I route_check.py gold.tsv $S/g2.tsv | tail -1","description":"Add the determinism scope to the README and make the scorer require explanations and reproducibility"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"540790d6-39c2-4bbf-ba85-0f155d32d591","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgjDRcAQxjVuio9F52qaj","requestRef":"a9ef7727-ae16-4edb-8398-9002877932de","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"afb31534-09a8-4d92-918d-de8647023ac6","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:18:13.105Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
