{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","id":"86285328-8c9c-4e42-a104-6e3e743efea0","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:18:36.301Z","version":"2.1.317","querySource":"repl_main_thread","shapeHash":"057cedc1f727758eac2aa8e2c7eab6e54ccaa77bb701c8037a06b043f3aeea83","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"f33ced78-a89a-4928-9fbf-2f2721095f85","keep":404,"tail":["376a1e719b2d372a683e9d1f4d8a675d389ecda5c9112b8b2902285aaf030cea","34c35fdc2d7f9e71655aa0ce3411a0ab0882de5d230b19d6f88d91b719a4f561"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",405,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"cbce95730c3e6bc163ac95cbf4d5a3777ef0b37aec363005c13d500e91cc64ec"}
{"parentUuid":"93062371-1e46-4384-a01f-645f09f13296","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDVKq1Uj5z42xna9vfW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Rescoped. I'm not writing to the plan, and the router is now deterministic, with no model making routing decisions. It's pushed to the dark repo (branch `claude/instruction-routing`, now `4bee267`) and saved in Entire Brain. A copy is in `~/tray/instruction-routing/`.\n\n**How routing works now:**\n- **It's a fixed function.** It takes an instruction and its context, and returns a plan item, destinations, and the IDs of the rules that fired. The same input always gives the same output.\n- **It routes only on explicit keys,** tried in this order:\n  1. something the instruction names: a plan item, primitive, claim or repo;\n  2. the plan item or thread it's replying to, which is how a follow-up like \"strip it out\" gets routed;\n  3. a versioned word list that maps terms to primitives. For example, \"margin\", \"embargo\" and \"licence\" map to privileged primitives.\n- **The rules are fixed, ordered and numbered.** Rule one sends anything privileged to the dark repo. The rule IDs on each route are its explanation.\n- **Nothing is guessed.** An instruction with no key goes into a single \"unrouted\" queue for you. Your answer is recorded as your override, and can add a word or key so the same case routes itself next time.\n- **A model can only suggest keys,** shown next to the instruction. Routing ignores a suggestion until you accept it.\n\n**The test enforces this.** It fails if any route lacks rule IDs, if a privileged instruction lands outside the dark repo, or if two runs on the same input differ by a single byte. I ran it in each state: with no router it fails, routes without explanations fail, and explained matching routes pass.\n\n**One gap remains: the test set has no context.** It holds each instruction's text but not what it was replying to. So for the 16 short follow-ups, it can only check that the router sends them to \"unrouted\" rather than guessing. Adding the replied-to message as a column would let those rows test real routing.\n\nThe handoff for the plan coordinator now describes the deterministic design too. No router is built yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1590,"cache_read_input_tokens":400053,"output_tokens":678,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1590,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":678,"cache_read_input_tokens":400053,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1590,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1590},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d8e787c9-5ffd-4f76-b0b0-e26ea81ff735","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgjDVKbsrdDbDW9j3roXH","requestRef":"86285328-8c9c-4e42-a104-6e3e743efea0","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b4725347-ecbe-4bc5-b1c5-653835fb622a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:18:45.802Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/srvo/dev/anthropic-pbc","sessionId":"c1e11076-829e-4b02-9641-6b48b095d475","version":"2.1.317","gitBranch":"ec-ai-corpus","slug":"calm-crunching-lovelace"}
